                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "faddf787-215d-356b-adba-bc905af4d43e",
                        "entry_id": "6311d5c2-ddf8-3da4-954c-a1d0454dbb68",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act by which something is shunned; avoidance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "379a94d1-89cc-4c10-a851-58f687510dfd",
                                "sense_id": "faddf787-215d-356b-adba-bc905af4d43e",
                                "text": "His mind began showering him with painful memories, forcing him to relive shunnings that stretched from elementary to high school and a procession of college roommates who'd ignore him after the first week."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48ba22f0-02d1-41be-aec7-b76c0998ac3e",
                                "sense_id": "faddf787-215d-356b-adba-bc905af4d43e",
                                "text": "Shunnings divided families, turning sisters and brothers into strangers ... . . even if the shunned one repented and returned home."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bba564b-4eb7-4477-911d-22bd5e044245",
                                "sense_id": "faddf787-215d-356b-adba-bc905af4d43e",
                                "text": "It was during one of my first “shunnings” that I learned a very valuable lesson. Playground politics, it seemed, dictated that while being shunned by the cool group, it was not acceptable behavior to start hanging around with the “non-cool” group."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
